      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should focus on how the colonial powers established the necessary framework for modern governance, regardless of the exploitation involved. Railroads and telegraphs, for instance, created integrated national markets and allowed for centralized administration, which are prerequisites for any modern state. Furthermore, the introduction of Western legal and bureaucratic systems, while often biased, provided a standardized structure for commerce and law that successor governments could adopt. These systems, however flawed, provided a level of institutional scaffolding that was previously absent.",
